WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
Ireland was never part
of the Roman Empire.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.130
No Roman towns, no Roman
roads, no Roman law.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.150
Power was split between perhaps
100 to 150 small kingdoms,

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.000
each with its own king.

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:17.230
Patrick is remembered as
this island's apostle.

6
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.260
Yet a chronicle entry for 431 names
a bishop sent there before him.

7
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.940
So who was really first to
bring Christianity to Ireland?

8
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.660
In this mission, you'll
read one line of Latin,

9
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.820
written within a few years
of the event it records.

10
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.630
Then you'll weigh up
other clues: sea routes,

11
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.760
borrowed words, and saints'
Lives written centuries later.

12
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.760
Your mission: find out
who was really first,

13
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.810
and how historians can tell.
